# intelligence-core — global rules

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router · React 19 · TypeScript 5
- Tailwind v4 (classes-only styling — see `99-tailwind-only.mdc`)
- Radix UI primitives wrapped under `src/components/primitives/`
- HeroUI v3 via `@intelligence/ui/heroui` + `@import "@heroui/styles"` in `globals.css` (after `tailwindcss`)
- Design tokens at `src/styles/tokens.css` + `src/styles/tokens.ts`
- GSAP via `@/lib/motion` (re-exports `@intelligence/motion`; init via `GsapProvider` in root layout)
- next-themes (`attribute="data-theme"`) for dark/light

## Layout

```
src/app/         App Router routes, layout, sw.ts (Serwist)
src/components/  primitives/ atoms/ molecules/ organisms/ templates/
src/lib/         cn.ts, icons/, motion/
src/styles/      tokens.css, tokens.ts
public/          manifest.webmanifest, icons/
docs/            design-system/, adr/, cowork/
```

## Hard rules

- Use the `cn()` helper for className composition. Never concatenate class strings manually.
- Tokens via Tailwind utilities only (`bg-bg`, `text-fg`, `rounded-md`, `shadow-mid`). No hex / rgb / px literals in components.
- Imports flow upward only: atom -> molecule -> organism -> template -> page.
- New components belong in the correct atomic folder and need a Storybook story.
- Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`...) — enforced by commitlint.

## Don't

- Don't add `*.module.css`, styled-components, emotion, or any CSS-in-JS.
- Don't import Radix packages outside `src/components/primitives/`.
- Don't hard-code colours, spacing, radii, durations, or easings — extend tokens instead.
